// ISE 754 — Fall 2026 workspace settings.
//
// Copied to ISE754/.vscode/settings.json during setup. It applies ONLY to the
// ISE754 folder, so it does not touch Julia or any other folder on your machine.
//
// "julia.executablePath" accepts a juliaup channel written as "+<channel>".
// Pinning it here means VS Code runs the course on Julia 1.12.6 even if your
// default Julia is a different version for other work.
//
// "julia.useCodeLens" turns off the Run | Above | Below | Debug buttons the Julia
// extension floats above every ## cell marker. In julialang.language-julia 1.219.2
// those buttons throw away the cell that was clicked and run whichever cell the
// text cursor happens to sit in, and clicking a button does not move the cursor --
// so the Run above one cell silently runs another, with no error to say so. Run a
// cell by clicking inside it and pressing Alt+Enter; the current cell stays
// outlined, so what will run is always visible.
//
// "files.readonlyInclude" marks the two received folders read-only IN THE EDITOR:
// you can open and read anything in them, and VS Code refuses to save a change.
// That is what they are -- materials/ and handouts/ are clones you pull, so an
// edit there is lost on the next update and, worse, makes the next `git pull`
// refuse. To try something out in a lecture's script, copy it to
// work/lectures/ and work on the copy; ask Claude Code and it will do that.
// The globs are relative to the ISE754 folder.
{
  "julia.executablePath": "+1.12.6",

  "julia.useCodeLens": false,

  "files.readonlyInclude": {
    "materials/**": true,
    "handouts/**": true
  }
}
